# English Vocabulary List — A0/A1 (Beginner) Level

**General-purpose word list for children, teens, adults, and seniors.**

- **Unique words in this list: 1158**
- Organized into **34 everyday topics**
- Built from standard beginner-level references: CEFR/English Vocabulary Profile (Cambridge), the Oxford 3000 A1 band, and typical general-English coursebook wordlists (family, numbers, food, house, school, travel, etc.)

> **A note on scope:** A true A0–A1 (beginner) vocabulary is, by definition, small — CEFR research (Cambridge English Profile, Oxford 3000, Paul Nation's frequency-band studies) puts real A1 vocabulary at roughly **500–1,000 words**. There is no genuine '10,000-word beginner list' — a list that size would already be intermediate/advanced (B2–C1) vocabulary. This document pushes the beginner list as far as it can reasonably go — combining core A1 with a generous A2 stretch — while keeping every word simple, concrete, and appropriate for a general course. If you want more raw volume after this, the natural next step is a labeled A2/B1 extension list.

